<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Certification of Trust - California</title>
    <style>
        /* ==========================================================================
           CERTIFICATION OF TRUST — Prob C §18100.5 — wave 1 #6

           Reference implementation: Pacific Coast Title blank form #72
           (Trust-Certification), measured with pdfplumber (letter page;
           recorder caption ~192pt; title below; one page + the ATTACHED
           §1189 acknowledgment — the reference's own foot directive reads
           "(Acknowledgement must be attached)", so the certificate rides
           as its own page via the partial's default mode).

           Family facts (FORMS_TRIAGE correction note): an ACKNOWLEDGED
           penalty-of-perjury declaration — never a jurat. PROPERTY-LESS:
           the instrument certifies a TRUST, not a parcel — no APN line,
           no legal description (the reference carries neither).

           OWNER RULING (wave-1 hold #3): the item-4 power lines and the
           item-5 Revocable/Irrevocable checkboxes are EXECUTION acts —
           initialing/checking is the trustee's hand at signing. They
           render BLANK, always (occurrence-pinned); a pre-marked power
           would be a fabricated assertion. The builder's typed
           transcriptions fill TEXT blanks only.

           Chassis rules (G2/G3) otherwise verbatim: §27361.6 open
           recorder space + boundary caption; §27361.7 no chrome;
           blank-contents doctrine for execution and notarial entries.
           ========================================================================== */

        @page {
            size: letter;
            margin: 0.5in 0.5in 0.6in 0.6in;
        }

        * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

        body {
            font-family: "Times New Roman", Times, Georgia, serif;
            font-size: 11pt;
            line-height: 1.35;
            color: #000;
            background: #fff;
        }

        .header-section { display: flex; min-height: 1.85in; }

        .recording-info {
            width: 3.4in;
            flex-shrink: 0;
            border-right: 0.75pt solid #000;
            padding-right: 0.15in;
            font-size: 10pt;
            line-height: 1.35;
        }

        .recorder-space { flex-grow: 1; }

        .recording-label {
            font-weight: bold;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            font-size: 9pt;
        }

        .recording-value { margin-bottom: 0.12in; min-height: 0.35in; }

        .ref-line { font-size: 10pt; }

        .header-boundary {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: flex-end;
            align-items: baseline;
            border-bottom: 0.75pt solid #000;
            padding-bottom: 0.03in;
            margin-bottom: 0.12in;
        }

        .recorder-caption {
            font-size: 7.5pt;
            font-weight: bold;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        .deed-title {
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 14pt;
            font-weight: bold;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            margin: 0.08in 0 0.02in 0;
        }

        .deed-subtitle {
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 10pt;
            font-weight: bold;
            margin-bottom: 0.08in;
        }

        .certification-body {
            font-size: 10.5pt;
            line-height: 1.3;
            text-align: justify;
        }

        .certification-body p { margin-bottom: 0.06in; }

        .cert-item { margin-bottom: 0.06in; }

        .cert-sub { margin-left: 0.35in; }

        .fact { font-weight: bold; }

        .fact-line {
            display: inline-block;
            min-width: 2in;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #000;
        }

        /* Execution-reserved marks (owner ruling): ALWAYS blank — the
           trustee initials/checks by hand at signing. */
        .initial-line {
            display: inline-block;
            width: 0.5in;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #000;
            margin-right: 0.08in;
        }

        .check-line {
            display: inline-block;
            width: 0.4in;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #000;
            margin: 0 0.06in;
        }

        .execution-section {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: flex-end;
            margin-top: 0.1in;
            margin-bottom: 0.04in;
        }

        .signature-block { width: 3.2in; }

        .signature-line {
            border-bottom: 1px solid #000;
            width: 3.2in;
            height: 0.3in;
        }

        .attach-directive {
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 9pt;
            font-weight: bold;
            margin-top: 0.08in;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="deed-page">

        <header class="header-section">
            <div class="recording-info">
                <div class="recording-label">Recording Requested By:</div>
                <div class="recording-value">{{ requested_by or '' }}{% if requested_by_address %}<br>{{ requested_by_address }}{% endif %}</div>

                <div class="recording-label">When Recorded Mail To:</div>
                <div class="recording-value">
                    {% if return_to %}
                        {% if return_to.get('name') %}{{ return_to.get('name') }}<br>{% endif %}
                        {% if return_to.get('company') %}{{ return_to.get('company') }}<br>{% endif %}
                        {# DEED-POLISH #1 — AN EMPTY LINE IS A PROMPT, A MISSING ONE IS
                           INVISIBLE (owner-ruled). A return-to with a name and no address
                           used to collapse to a single line, which reads as complete. A
                           partner with no address on file now leaves a visible rule, the
                           same convention the reference numbers and the no-return-to
                           branch below already use. #}
                        {% set _ret_addr = return_to.get('address1') or return_to.get('address2')
                                           or return_to.get('city') or return_to.get('state')
                                           or return_to.get('zip') %}
                        {% if not _ret_addr %}_________________________________<br>
                        _________________________________{% endif %}
                        {% if return_to.get('address1') %}{{ return_to.get('address1') }}<br>{% endif %}
                        {% if return_to.get('address2') %}{{ return_to.get('address2') }}<br>{% endif %}
                        {% set city = return_to.get('city', '') %}
                        {% set state = return_to.get('state', '') %}
                        {% set zip = return_to.get('zip', '') %}
                        {% if city or state or zip %}
                            {{ city }}{% if city and (state or zip) %}, {% endif %}{{ state }} {{ zip }}
                        {% endif %}
                    {% else %}
                        _________________________________<br>
                        _________________________________<br>
                        _________________________________
                    {% endif %}
                </div>

                <div class="ref-line">Order No.: {{ title_order_no or '____________________' }}</div>
                <div class="ref-line">Escrow No.: {{ escrow_no or '____________________' }}</div>
            </div>

            <div class="recorder-space"><!-- Gov. Code §27361.6 — recorder's use only --></div>
        </header>

        {# Property-less instrument: no APN on the boundary — caption only,
           as the reference prints it. #}
        <div class="header-boundary">
            <span class="recorder-caption">Space Above This Line Is For Recorder&rsquo;s Use</span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="deed-title">Certification of Trust</h1>
        <div class="deed-subtitle">California Probate Code Section 18100.5</div>

        {% set aff = affidavit or {} %}
        <div class="certification-body">
            <p>
                The undersigned declare(s) under penalty of perjury under the laws of the State
                of California that the following is true and correct:
            </p>

            <div class="cert-item">
                1. The Trust known as
                {% if aff.get('trust_name') %}<span class="fact">{{ aff.get('trust_name') }}</span>{% else %}<span class="fact-line" style="min-width:3in">&nbsp;</span>{% endif %},
                executed on {% if aff.get('trust_date') %}<span class="fact">{{ aff.get('trust_date') }}</span>{% else %}<span class="fact-line" style="min-width:1.4in">&nbsp;</span>{% endif %},
                is a valid and existing trust.
            </div>

            <div class="cert-item">
                2. The name(s) of the settlor(s) of the Trust is (are):
                {% if aff.get('settlors') %}<span class="fact">{{ aff.get('settlors') }}</span>{% else %}<span class="fact-line" style="min-width:3in">&nbsp;</span>{% endif %}
            </div>

            <div class="cert-item">
                3. The name(s) of the currently acting trustee(s) is (are):
                {% if aff.get('trustees') %}<span class="fact">{{ aff.get('trustees') }}</span>{% else %}<span class="fact-line" style="min-width:3in">&nbsp;</span>{% endif %}
            </div>

            <div class="cert-item">
                4. The trustee(s) of the Trust have the following powers (initial applicable line(s)):
                <div class="cert-sub"><span class="initial-line">&nbsp;</span>Power to acquire additional property.</div>
                <div class="cert-sub"><span class="initial-line">&nbsp;</span>Power to sell and execute deeds.</div>
                <div class="cert-sub"><span class="initial-line">&nbsp;</span>Power to encumber, and execute deeds of trust.</div>
                <div class="cert-sub"><span class="initial-line">&nbsp;</span>Other: <span class="fact-line" style="min-width:3in">&nbsp;</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="cert-item">
                5. The Trust is (check one): <span class="check-line">&nbsp;</span>Revocable
                <span class="check-line">&nbsp;</span>Irrevocable
                <div>
                    The name of the person who may revoke the Trust is:
                    {% if aff.get('revoker_name') %}<span class="fact">{{ aff.get('revoker_name') }}</span>{% else %}<span class="fact-line" style="min-width:2.6in">&nbsp;</span>{% endif %}
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="cert-item">
                6. The number of trustees who must sign documents in order to exercise the powers
                of the Trust is (are):
                {% if aff.get('signer_count') %}<span class="fact">{{ aff.get('signer_count') }}</span>{% else %}<span class="fact-line" style="min-width:0.7in">&nbsp;</span>{% endif %},
                whose name(s) is (are):
                {% if aff.get('signer_names') %}<span class="fact">{{ aff.get('signer_names') }}</span>{% else %}<span class="fact-line" style="min-width:2.6in">&nbsp;</span>{% endif %}
            </div>

            <div class="cert-item">
                7. Title to Trust assets is to be taken as follows:
                {% if aff.get('title_vesting') %}<span class="fact">{{ aff.get('title_vesting') }}</span>{% else %}<span class="fact-line" style="min-width:3in">&nbsp;</span>{% endif %}
            </div>

            <div class="cert-item">
                8. The Trust has not been revoked, modified or amended in any manner which would
                cause the representations contained herein to be incorrect.
            </div>

            <div class="cert-item">9. I (we) am (are) all of the currently acting trustees.</div>

            <div class="cert-item">
                10. I (we) understand that I (we) may be required to provide copies of excerpts
                from the original Trust documents which designate the trustees and confer the
                power to act in the pending transaction.
            </div>
        </div>

        {# Execution: the trustee(s) sign at notarization — dates,
           signatures, initials, and checkmarks are theirs (blank-contents
           + the owner's execution-acts ruling). #}
        <div class="execution-section">
            <div>Dated: <span class="fact-line" style="min-width:1.8in">&nbsp;</span></div>
            <div class="signature-block">
                <div class="signature-line" style="margin-bottom:0.15in"></div>
                <div class="signature-line"></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="attach-directive">(Acknowledgement must be attached)</div>

    </div>

    {# The attached §1189 certificate — the partial's own-page default IS
       the attachment the foot directive demands. #}
    {% set document_title = 'Certification of Trust' %}
    {% include '_partials/notary_acknowledgment.jinja2' %}

</body>
</html>
